      <title>RAG systems: evidence, evaluation, and uncertainty</title>
      <link>https://chikuang.github.io/resources/rag_system/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://chikuang.github.io/resources/rag_system/</guid>
      <description>&lt;style&gt;&#xA;#resource-body table { display: block; max-width: 100%; overflow-x: auto; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 0.75rem 0; }&#xA;#resource-body th, #resource-body td { padding: 0.35rem 0.5rem; vertical-align: top; }&#xA;#resource-body .code-fold { margin: 0.75rem 0; }&#xA;#resource-body .code-fold &gt; summary { display: list-item; list-style-position: inside; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; }&#xA;#resource-body .code-fold &gt; summary:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid currentColor; outline-offset: 4px; }&#xA;#resource-body .code-fold pre { margin-top: 0.5rem; }&#xA;#resource-body .text-fold { margin: 0.75rem 0 1.2rem; }&#xA;#resource-body .text-fold &gt; summary { display: list-item; list-style-position: inside; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; }&#xA;#resource-body .text-fold &gt; summary:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid currentColor; outline-offset: 4px; }&#xA;#resource-body .text-fold &gt; ul, #resource-body .text-fold &gt; ol { margin-top: 0.65rem; }&#xA;#resource-body .rag-illustration { margin: 1.1rem 0 1.4rem; }&#xA;#resource-body .rag-illustration--plan { max-width: 560px; margin-inline: auto; }&#xA;#resource-body .rag-illustration &gt; a { display: block; border-radius: 12px; }&#xA;#resource-body .rag-illustration img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 12px; }&#xA;#resource-body .rag-illustration figcaption { margin-top: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.9em; line-height: 1.5; }&#xA;#resource-body .illustration-credit { display: block; margin-top: 0.2rem; font-size: 0.85em; opacity: 0.75; }&#xA;&lt;/style&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A useful research assistant should show where its answer comes from—and recognize when the available evidence is not enough.&lt;/strong&gt; Retrieval-augmented generation (&lt;strong&gt;RAG&lt;/strong&gt;) connects a language model to an external collection of documents. Instead of answering only from information encoded in its parameters, the model receives retrieved passages as context for its response. Lewis et al. introduced a prominent framework combining a neural retriever with a generative model. &lt;a href=&#34;#ref-rag&#34;&gt;[1]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
